WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.940
In 1960, five oil-exporting
countries set up OPEC.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.630
Its members agree on production targets
to influence the world oil price.

3
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.580
In the US, firms that fix
prices together break the law,

4
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.210
under the Sherman Act of 1890.

5
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.240
Yet when only a few big
firms share a market,

6
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.650
their prices often move together.

7
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:25.480
Why? In this mission, you'll
see why oligopolists have

8
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.620
an incentive to collude and form a cartel.

9
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.710
Then you'll test, in a graph lab,

10
00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.840
whether breaking the
cartel's deal pays off.

11
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.400
Your mission: explain why
a few big firms' prices

12
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.550
so often stay close together.
